          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+compactification"} flux compactification
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptically fibered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+variety"} Calabi-Yau variety
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"}> complex
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            4 (hence real dimension 8, see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+8-manifolds"} M-theory on 8-manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+superstring+theory"} type IIB superstring theory
            (with some
            = succeed "-related" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effects"} non-perturbative effects
            included)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactified
            on Calabi-Yau 3-folds.
          %p
            This is subtly different from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory+on+Spin%287%29-manifolds"} F-theory on Spin(7)-manifolds
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten%27s+Dark+Fantasy"} Witten's Dark Fantasy
          %p
            Realization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stabilization"} moduli stabilization
            of those flux compactifications is by considering higher dimensional gauge fields in the compact space, the curvature of those fields parametrizes the mass term.
          %h3#motivation_from_string_model_buildingphenomenology Motivation from string model building/phenomenology
          %p
            By the discussion at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+and+Calabi-Yau+manifolds"} supersymmetry and Calabi-Yau manifolds
            such compactifications of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+superstring+theory"} type IIB superstring theory
            yield the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UV-completion"} UV-completion
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            in 4-dimensions which exhibits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N =1
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
          %div
            %p
              %strong>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactifications"} KK-compactifications
                of higher dimensional
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
                with minimal (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
                ) supersymmetry
              \:
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th perspective
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
                    with
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory+on+CY4-manifolds"} F-theory on CY4-manifolds
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory+on+CY3-manifolds"} heterotic string theory on CY3-manifolds
          %p
            For this reason F/M-theory compactifications on elliptically fibered Calabi-Yau 4-folds are a major contender in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28physics%29"} model
            building. See at
            %em
              %a{:href => "string+phenomenology#ModelsInTypeIIWithIntersectingBranes"} string phenomenology – Models in type II / F-theory
            for more on this.
          %h3#motivation_from_mathematics Motivation from mathematics
          %p
            At the same time these types of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactifications"} KK-compactifications
            are of interest also for their pure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            and as such received a fair amount of attention notably in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
          %p
            For instance the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+F-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory"} duality between F-theory and heterotic string theory
            translates into a class of rich equivalences of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            of bundles on different
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+varieties"} algebraic varieties
            which is rather non-obvious without the
            = succeed "-perspective." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %p
            From the abstract of (
            %a{:href => "#Donagi98"}> Donagi 98
            ).
          %blockquote
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactified
              on an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptically fibered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+variety"} Calabi-Yau
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \to B
              is conjectured to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} dual
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactified
              on an
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+variety"} Calabi-Yau
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
              fibers. In particular, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli"} moduli
              of the two theories should be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=2
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactification
              is to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensions"} dimensions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 8
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d=8
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 6
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 6
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4
              respectively. Mathematically, the richest picture seems to emerge for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=3
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
              involves an analytically
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+system"} integrable system
              whose fibers admit rather different descriptions in the two theories.
          %p
            Moreover, the description of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            (in the physics literature: the “4-form flux”, see at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+compactification"} flux compactification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in degree-4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+variety"} Calabi-Yau variety
            involves the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces+of+%28higher%29+line+bundles"} moduli spaces of (higher) line bundles
            on the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CY
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CY_4
            which under decomposition of the C-field into various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product+in+ordinary+differential+cohomology"} cup-product
            factors associated with the various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divisor+%28algebraic+geometry%29"} divisor
            of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CY
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CY_4
            involves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+Jacobians"} intermediate Jacobians
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin-Mazur+formal+groups"} Artin-Mazur formal groups
            in degrees 0,1,2 with rich theory.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactified
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptically fibered
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+space"} complex analytic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi dim
                            %mi ℂ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim_{\mathbb{C}}(\Sigma)
                  %th 1
                  %th 2
                  %th 3
                  %th 4
                  %th 5
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+2-folds"} F-theory on CY2
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+3-folds"} F-theory on CY3
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+4-folds"} F-theory on CY4
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+5-folds"} F-theory on CY5
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory+on+Spin%287%29-manifolds"} F-theory on Spin(7)-manifolds
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+a+circle"} M-theory on a circle
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+8-manifolds"}> M-theory on 8-manifolds
                  \/
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+Spin%287%29-manifolds"} on Spin(7)-manifolds
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
                %ul
                  %li
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-MSSM"} G₂-MSSM
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+Sp%281%29-manifolds"} M-theory on Sp(1)-manifolds
              %li
                %p
