                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+5-folds"} on CY5-folds
          %h2#references References
          %p Reviews of the general setup include
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Grimm"}> Thomas Grimm
              , Raffaele Savelli, sections 3.1, 3.2 of
              %em Gravitational Instantons and Fluxes from M/F-theory on Calabi-Yau fourfolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1109.3191"}> arXiv:1109.3191
              )
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+F-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory"} duality between F-theory and heterotic string theory
            for compactifications on elliptically fibered Calabi-Yau manifolds includes
          %ul
            %li#Donagi98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ron+Donagi"}> Ron Donagi
                ,
                %em ICMP lecture on heterotic/F-theory duality
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9802093"}> arXiv:hep-th/9802093
                )
            %li#DonagiMarkman95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ron+Donagi"}> Ron Donagi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eyal+Markman"} Eyal Markman
                %em Spectral curves, algebraically completely integrable Hamiltonian systems, and moduli of bundles
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9507017"}> arXiv:alg-geom/9507017
                )
          %p
            Discussion of relation to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+Spin%288%29-manifolds"} M-theory on Spin(8)-manifolds
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mariana+Gra%C3%B1a"}> Mariana Graña
              , C. S. Shahbazi,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Zambon"} Marco Zambon
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 7
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(7)
                  \-manifolds in compactifications to four dimensions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1405.3698"} arXiv:1405.3698
          %p
